\\infty ,2).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{3}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/80/808abeaa59d7bcea3b24e741fde5296791de32b4170d60f05f2a5af203c20ba2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in [0,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{t+1} \\\\ {e}^{t} \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b637ea2-eaa0-55d8-b435-a20c614987db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281528 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t+1}$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $2t$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f1ca1c3d6ffd56fe0686ee209c967775b5daf09a99e80a3f38ad0a56f4424ce.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162685" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-4}\\,i+t\\,j+\\sqrt{t-2}\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49867506-48a9-52ef-9b83-53c3f3a13af0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281530 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the ind